00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.570
I'm From Brazil

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.940
Hello, konnichiwa!

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.600
I came from Brazil!

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.570
K-K-Konnichiwa! S-São Paolo!

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.090
<b>Audio</b>

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.090
<b>Japanese</b>

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:42.100
There's something I wanted 
to ask you, actually.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.370
<i>All right, bring it!</i>

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.800
<i>I'll help you out so well.</i>

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.550
Comics in Europe and the US are all colorful,

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.880
but Japanese manga are all black and white.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.070
Why?

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.180
I don't know!

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.580
Oh, I wasn't looking for <i>the</i> answer.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.920
I just wanted to hear a 
Japanese person's opinion.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.420
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.530
<i>But I'll have to do what I can.</i>

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:27.210
Let's! Bullshit English Time

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.830
I think

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.100
colorful comics are expensive to publish.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.330
Japanese manga is cheaper than that.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.570
So... I'm not sure,

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:24.410
but cutting costs is one of the reasons...

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.210
I um, err, eh, I think? Probably, yeah, maybe...

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.650
I got it!

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.650
<i>Wait, seriously?!</i>

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.770
Thank you, that was interesting!

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.120
That makes sense!

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.990
One last thing, then...

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.200
